WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.090
Many holy people have
left the world behind,

2
00:00:03.140 --> 00:00:06.400
to seek God alone in caves and forests.

3
00:00:06.450 --> 00:00:09.850
Yet in Guru Nanak's own
community, Sikhs prayed,

4
00:00:09.900 --> 00:00:12.660
farmed and shared their meals together.

5
00:00:12.710 --> 00:00:16.400
A Sikh story even has him turn
down a rich official's feast,

6
00:00:16.450 --> 00:00:18.900
to eat a poor carpenter's bread.

7
00:00:18.950 --> 00:00:23.360
So why would a religion that seeks union
with God insist that you go out and earn

8
00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:24.720
a living?

9
00:00:24.770 --> 00:00:28.370
In this mission, you'll meet
three pillars of Sikh life.

10
00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:30.800
Then you'll read two
verses that join them,

11
00:00:30.850 --> 00:00:33.640
and test them on real choices at work.

12
00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:38.840
Your mission: find out why Sikhs who
seek God insist on earning a living.
